# Line endings, made explicit so they stop being a source of confusion.
#
# The tree was developed on Windows: 36 files under google-maps-scraper/ differ
# from upstream only by CRLF. Committing that as-is would show those files as
# modified for everyone else. So: text files are stored and checked out as LF,
# except the two Windows entry scripts, which cmd.exe wants in CRLF.
#
# The .bat file must stay CRLF with no BOM -- cmd.exe's parser drifts otherwise
# (see collector/collector/launcher.py). Enforcing it here keeps a "normalise
# line endings" commit from quietly breaking the double-click entry.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
